    "# 🏗️ Entity Preparation Pipeline v3\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📖 Introduction to Entity Resolution\n",
    "\n",
    "**What is Entity Resolution?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Entity resolution is the problem of identifying when different mentions in text refer to the same real-world entity. This is a fundamental challenge in information extraction, data integration, and knowledge management.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Real-World Examples:**\n",
    "- \"The President\" → \"Joe Biden\" (when context indicates US politics)\n",
    "- \"Vladimir Putin\" → \"Vladimir Vladimirovich Putin\" (full name vs. common name)\n",
    "- \"Apple\" → Could be \"Apple Inc.\" (company) or \"apple\" (fruit) - context matters!\n",
    "- \"J. Smith\" → \"John Smith\" (abbreviation expansion)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why It Matters:**\n",
    "- **Information Extraction**: Finding and linking entities across documents\n",
    "- **Watch List Monitoring**: Tracking sanctioned individuals or entities across news sources\n",
    "- **News Analysis**: Identifying when different articles mention the same person or organization\n",
    "- **Data Integration**: Merging records from different sources that refer to the same entity\n",
    "\n",
    "**High-Level Approach: Three-Stage Pipeline**\n",
    "\n",
    "Our entity resolution system uses a three-stage pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Entity Preparation** (This notebook) - Prepare entities for matching by enriching them with context and indexing them\n",
    "2. **Article Processing** (Notebook 2) - Extract entities from articles and text\n",
    "3. **Entity Matching** (Notebook 3) - Match extracted entities to prepared entities using AI-powered judgment\n",
    "\n",
    "Each stage builds upon the previous one, creating a complete entity resolution system.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔄 Pipeline Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "The entity resolution pipeline consists of three interconnected stages that work together to solve the entity resolution problem:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│                    Entity Resolution Pipeline                     │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "\n",
    "Stage 1: Entity Preparation (This Notebook)\n",
    "├── EntityWatchList: Manage entities to monitor\n",
    "├── EntityEnricher: Add context from Wikipedia\n",
    "└── EntityIndexer: Index entities in Elasticsearch\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "    [Elasticsearch Index]\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "Stage 2: Article Processing (Notebook 2)\n",
    "├── ArticleProcessor: Load and process articles\n",
    "└── HybridNERExtractor: Extract entities from text\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "    [Extracted Entities]\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "Stage 3: Entity Matching (Notebook 3)\n",
    "├── ElasticsearchEntityMatcher: Find potential matches\n",
    "└── LLM Judge: Make final match decisions\n",
    "        │\n",
    "        ▼\n",
    "    [Entity Matches]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data Flow:**\n",
    "- **Entities** → Prepared with context → Indexed in Elasticsearch\n",
    "- **Articles** → Processed → Entities extracted\n",
    "- **Extracted Entities** → Matched against prepared entities → Matches confirmed\n",
    "\n",
    "**What Each Stage Produces:**\n",
    "- **Stage 1 (Entity Preparation)**: Searchable index of entities with rich context\n",
    "- **Stage 2 (Article Processing)**: List of entities extracted from articles\n",
    "- **Stage 3 (Entity Matching)**: Confirmed matches between extracted and prepared entities\n",
    "\n",
    "**How Notebooks Connect:**\n",
    "- Notebook 1 (this notebook) creates the entity index that Notebook 3 uses for matching\n",
    "- Notebook 2 extracts entities from articles that Notebook 3 matches against the prepared entities\n",
    "- Notebook 3 completes the pipeline by matching entities using the prepared index\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🎯 Problem → Solution → Components\n",
    "\n",
    "### **The Problem**\n",
    "\n",
    "In entity resolution, we need to match entities mentioned in text (like \"The Russian President\") to known entities in our watch list (like \"Vladimir Putin\"). However, entities can be mentioned in many different ways:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Different names**: \"Vladimir Putin\" vs \"Vladimir Vladimirovich Putin\"\n",
    "- **Titles and roles**: \"The President\" vs \"Vladimir Putin\"\n",
    "- **Abbreviations**: \"J. Smith\" vs \"John Smith\"\n",
    "- **Different languages**: \"北京\" vs \"Beijing\"\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Why Entity Preparation Matters**\n",
    "\n",
    "**What happens if we skip entity preparation?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Without proper entity preparation, matching becomes unreliable:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **No Context**: We can't match \"The Russian President\" to \"Vladimir Putin\" because we don't know what \"The Russian President\" means\n",
    "- **No Aliases**: We can't match \"F.D.R.\" to \"Franklin Delano Roosevelt\" because we don't know they're the same person\n",
    "- **No Semantic Search**: We can't match \"Tesla CEO\" to \"Elon Musk\" because we can't understand the semantic relationship\n",
    "- **Poor Performance**: Without indexing, every match requires scanning all entities, which is slow and inefficient\n",
    "\n",
    "**What entity preparation enables:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Context-Aware Matching**: Wikipedia context helps match titles and roles to specific entities\n",
    "- **Alias Recognition**: Known aliases enable matching name variations\n",
    "- **Semantic Understanding**: Semantic embeddings enable matching based on meaning, not just text\n",
    "- **Fast Search**: Elasticsearch indexing enables fast, scalable matching\n",
    "\n",
    "### **Our Solution**\n",
    "\n",
    "A three-component entity preparation system that:\n",
    "1. **Manages entities** (EntityWatchList) - Organizes entities and their metadata\n",
    "2. **Enriches entities** (EntityEnricher) - Adds context from Wikipedia to help with matching\n",
    "3. **Indexes entities** (EntityIndexer) - Creates a searchable index in Elasticsearch with semantic search capabilities\n",
    "\n",
    "### **The Components**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the three-component entity preparation pipeline:\n",
    "- **EntityWatchList**: Entity management and metadata handling\n",
    "- **EntityEnricher**: Context enhancement with Wikipedia and multilingual support\n",
    "- **EntityIndexer**: Elasticsearch integration with semantic search capabilities\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ **Required**: Elasticsearch connection with E5 model for semantic search  \n",
    "✅ **Required**: Python environment with required packages  \n",
    "✅ **Required**: Minimal entities dataset (`notebooks/minimal_entities.json`)  \n",
    "\n",
    "**Note**: This notebook uses the real implementation of all components, not simulations.\n",
    "\n",
