    "## 6. EntityIndexer: Elasticsearch Integration\n",
    "\n",
    "The EntityIndexer creates searchable Elasticsearch indices with semantic mappings, enabling hybrid search capabilities for entity matching.\n",
    "\n",
    "<details>\n",
    "<summary><strong>💡 Understanding Semantic Search</strong> (Click to expand)</summary>\n",
    "\n",
    "**What is Semantic Search?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Semantic search finds entities by meaning, not just keywords. For example, \"Russian President\" can match \"Vladimir Putin\" even without exact text match. This is crucial for entity resolution because entities can be mentioned in many different ways.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What are Embeddings?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Embeddings convert text into numerical vectors (arrays of numbers) that capture meaning. Similar meanings result in similar vectors, allowing the system to find \"Russian President\" when searching for \"Vladimir Putin\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**The E5 Model**\n",
    "\n",
    "Elasticsearch uses the E5 (EmbEddings from bidirEctional Encoder rEpresentations) model to automatically generate embeddings. When you index text in a `semantic_text` field, Elasticsearch automatically:\n",
    "1. Converts the text to an embedding vector\n",
    "2. Stores the vector in the index\n",
    "3. Enables semantic similarity search\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why This Matters for Entity Resolution**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Title Matching**: \"The President\" can match \"Joe Biden\" through semantic understanding\n",
    "- **Context-Aware**: \"Russian leader\" matches \"Vladimir Putin\" based on meaning\n",
    "- **Multilingual**: Works across languages when combined with other techniques\n",
    "- **Fuzzy Matching**: Handles variations and paraphrases that keyword search would miss\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learn more:** [Elasticsearch Semantic Search Guide](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/semantic-search.html)\n",
    "\n",
    "</details>\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔍 **EntityIndexer Architecture**\n",
    "\n",
    "The EntityIndexer provides:\n",
    "- **Index Creation**: Elasticsearch indices with semantic mappings\n",
    "- **Entity Indexing**: Bulk indexing of enriched entities\n",
    "- **Index Verification**: Validation of index structure and content\n",
    "- **Statistics**: Comprehensive indexing statistics and monitoring\n",
    "\n",
    "### 📊 **What You'll Learn**\n",
    "\n",
    "- How Elasticsearch indices are created with semantic mappings\n",
    "- How entities are indexed for efficient search\n",
    "- How index verification ensures data integrity\n",
    "- Performance characteristics of indexing operations\n"
   ]
