    "## 🔄 Why We Need Saved State\n",
    "\n",
    "The entity preparation pipeline creates a **saved state** that serves as the foundation for the entire entity resolution system. This state file is critical for pipeline continuity and enables downstream processing.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🎯 **What the State Enables**\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. Article Processing Pipeline** (`02_article_processing_v3.ipynb`)\n",
    "- **Entity Context**: Articles need to know which entities to look for\n",
    "- **Alias Matching**: Articles contain entity references that may use aliases\n",
    "- **Entity Types**: Articles need to understand entity categories for proper extraction\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. Entity Matching Pipeline** (`03_entity_matching_v3.ipynb`)\n",
    "- **Search Targets**: The matching system needs to know what entities to search for\n",
    "- **Enriched Context**: Matching uses the enriched Wikipedia context for semantic similarity\n",
    "- **Alias Resolution**: Matching needs aliases to find entities mentioned by different names\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. Pipeline Continuity**\n",
    "- **No Re-processing**: Downstream notebooks don't need to re-run entity preparation\n",
    "- **Consistent State**: All notebooks work with the same entity data\n",
    "- **Performance**: Avoids redundant API calls to Wikipedia and Elasticsearch\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔗 **State File Structure**\n",
    "\n",
    "The state file contains everything needed for downstream processing:\n",
    "- **Entity Definitions**: Names, types, descriptions, and aliases\n",
    "- **Enriched Context**: Wikipedia context for semantic matching\n",
    "- **Metadata**: Processing timestamps, confidence scores, and statistics\n",
    "- **Index Information**: Elasticsearch index names and document counts\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🚀 **Next Steps**\n",
    "\n",
    "This state file will be used by:\n",
    "1. **Article Processing** - To extract entities from articles\n",
    "2. **Entity Matching** - To find and match entities in text\n",
    "3. **Complete Pipeline** - To orchestrate the entire entity resolution workflow\n"
